      "message": "I respect the author of the original change, but this change is mostly cleanup of the remaining PASR / mem-offline bits.\n\nThe original commit was not directly applicable to my case. I spent roughly two months debugging the issue and found the actual cause independently.\n\nAlso, I am specifically referring to **Patchset 2** of the referenced change: it was updated after my fix, and some additions there overlap with changes I had already made. I am not claiming that the whole original change was based on my work.\n\nFor reference:\n\n* https://review.lineageos.org/q/topic:%22fsa4480-supply-mode%22\n* https://review.lineageos.org/c/LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8450-devicetrees/+/492920\n\nSo I don\u0027t think it is entirely correct to attribute this cleanup to that commit alone.\n\nThat said, I don\u0027t really care who is listed as the author. My main concern is that the final implementation is correct and works. I\u0027d rather not spend more time arguing about authorship for what is essentially cleanup.",
